    "result_text": "Done. The build is green.\n\nI implemented `initials` with minimal structural impact by touching just two files and one function:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `readOnly` `initials` string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field (and it serializes into the GET response). No functions changed here.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added one `@Mapping` line to the existing `toOwnerDto` method (CC 1, small surrounding interface), computing the value inline:\n   ```\n   owner.getFirstName().substring(0,1).toUpperCase() + \".\" + owner.getLastName().substring(0,1).toUpperCase() + \".\"\n   ```\n\nThis mirrors how the existing `displayName` field is derived, so it fits the established pattern. I deliberately avoided adding a method to the large `Owner` entity, which would have paid the whole class's WMC as surrounding-context cost. `john`/`smith` \u2192 `J.S.`, test passes.",
